00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.900
Now the thing about raw chicken is whenever you use it, or whenever you cut with it, you

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.220
always want to make sure that you don't cross-contaminate.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:54.810
So what I'm going to do is take this cutting board that we just cut the chicken on and

00:03:54.810 --> 00:04:00.000
put it aside, and I'm going to start with a new cutting board to cut it.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.080
all the vegetables with because you don't want to get the raw chicken into the vegetables that's

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.580
what you call cross contamination and sometimes you hear about salmonella poisoning and in

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:15.120
restaurants especially that's what happens somebody will be working on one item and uh go to another

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:19.500
item so even i touch the thing i'm going to take off these gloves and that's the reason for the

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.340
