00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.500
a peel and just peel both sides off and we're actually just going to use a little bit of onion

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:59.410
in this so i only actually need one half let me get rid of all the scraps put those aside and

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:06.540
On the onion, we want to cut julienne, which is a long thin strip. Julienne is like a matchstick.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:12.460
It's a two-inch thin strip. So just putting the knife against the onion straight down.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:19.380
You're cutting thin strips, and then the onion will naturally fall apart into nice thin strips.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:29.690
So I'm just going to cut this whole end here, and we'll put the onion aside.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:35.840
