00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:17.700
butter we don't want too much butter but we want enough so the chicken doesn't

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:25.770
stick and you can see that pan got nice and hot really quick as soon as the

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:30.000
butter melts there's a lot of water in butter you know that old miss muffler

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.580
it sat on the top of it eating in the curds and whey. If you were to melt butter in a pan,

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:39.770
you'd see the top would be yellow. That's the butter fat. And on the bottom is the curds

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:45.310
and the whey, and there's actually water in butter. So as the water, as the butter heats

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:49.850
up, you can see it sizzling. That's the water trying to evaporate. So that's what happens

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:54.760
there. But once it gets melted like that, you just want to lay the chicken in. And I

00:11:54.760 --> 00:12:00.000
always lay it in and I push it away from me. That way there, if it does splash, it'll

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:09.500
